Per-plugin asset directories live here:

  docs/assets/plugins/depth_da3/
  docs/assets/plugins/normal_crafter/
  docs/assets/plugins/depth_crafter/
  docs/assets/plugins/segmentation_sam3/
  docs/assets/plugins/matte_mama/
  docs/assets/plugins/matte_ma2/
  docs/assets/plugins/upscale_seedvr2/

Each will hold:
  - hero.{jpg,png,webp}    : the plugin's primary doc image (top of page).
  - example-N.{jpg,png}    : additional example imagery.
  - parameters.{jpg,png}   : screenshot of the parameters panel in a host.
  - workflow.{jpg,png}     : the underlying ComfyUI workflow.

License note for image sourcing:

The research briefs in /contrib/release-staging/_research/ identified upstream
images that would be ideal for each plugin's documentation. With few
exceptions, those upstream sources do NOT permit redistribution under our
BSD-3-Clause license.

Recommended approach for each plugin:
  1. Generate fresh example output by running the plugin on CC0 / owned
     plates.
  2. Capture parameter-panel and workflow screenshots from a real host
     session.
  3. Save the resulting JPG/PNG into this directory and reference from the
     plugin's docs/plugins/<plugin>.md page.
  4. Reserve upstream images for "see also" link-outs only, with proper
     attribution.

Once images are added to each subdirectory, this .placeholder file can be
removed and the subdirectory itself will be tracked by Jekyll.
